{
    "background_story": "Enzo was a rare and exotic geophyte, a type of plant that stores its nutrients in underground tubers. He spent most of his life beneath the earth's surface, slowly growing and developing his unique characteristics. Enzo's home was in the arid desert landscape, where he had adapted to survive the harsh conditions. During the brief rainy season, he would burst forth from the ground, unfurling his delicate petals and revealing his vibrant colors. The local botanists were fascinated by Enzo's ability to thrive in such a challenging environment and would often visit him to study his remarkable geophytic traits. As the dry season returned, Enzo would retreat back into the earth, his tubers conserving energy for the next year's bloom, a testament to his remarkable resilience and adaptability.",
